# Company ids handed from the SEEDERS to the VERIFIERS on disk.
#
# `pnpm seed:demo` writes .demo-company-id and `pnpm seed:tenancy` writes
# .tenancy-company-id; `make seed-all` chains them and `pnpm verify:demo` /
# `pnpm verify:tenancy` take the ids as argv. They are per-machine, per-wipe
# throwaway UUIDs — committing one would point the next person's verify run at a
# company that does not exist in their database.
.demo-company-id
.tenancy-company-id
